#   python3 tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/hearthandharvest-common.toml crow stealChance 1.0
#   python3 tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/hearthandharvest-common.toml crow carryTicks 200
#   python3 tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/loadingprotection-common.toml '"Loading Protection Configuration"' protectionDuration 1
#   Wise Oak config untouched (defaults: SQ-WO-01 values).
# Probes to copy into OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/ (zq_probe.js is copied by prep_srv.sh):
#   cp tools/scratch_query/wo_probe.js        OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_wo_probe.js       (/zwo; also skip for SQ-HCS-05)
#   cp tools/scratch_query/hh_crow_probe.js   OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_hh_crow_probe.js  (/zhh3)
#   cp tools/scratch_query/hh_gear_probe.js   OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_hh_gear_probe.js  (/zhh5)
#   cp tools/scratch_query/zsneak_probe.js    OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_zsneak_probe.js   (/zsneak, new r1113)
# Coordinates: x 30000 to 31200, z 30000 to 30100 (clear of the chunk-4 batches). Keep the world for rerun_a2.qb.
pace 1

## SQ-RRA-00 | setup: forceload, bot G, gamerules (not a test row)
bootexpect Done \(
> forceload add 30000 29990 30200 30060
> forceload add 30480 29980 30560 30060
> forceload add 30980 29980 31080 30060
sleep 10
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> time set noon
> weather clear 100000
> pbot spawn G 30010 -60 30010 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> pbot status
expect cdevperfbot ok

## SQ-WO-03 | trust command errors (r1109 fault: an offline server resolves any plain name; use a selector that matches nobody)
> wiseoak trust 30030 -60 30020 G 50
> setblock 30030 -60 30020 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak
> wiseoak trust 30030 -60 30020 G 101
> wiseoak trust 30030 -60 30020 G -1
> wiseoak trust 30030 -60 30020 @a[name=Nobody123] 50
> wiseoak trust 99999 -60 99999 G 50
> setblock 30030 -60 30020 minecraft:stone
> wiseoak trust 30030 -60 30020 G 50
sleep 2
count No Wise Oak at that position == 2
expect (?i)integer must not be more than 100
expect (?i)integer must not be less than 0
expect No player was found|That player does not exist
expect That position is not loaded
reject Set trust of Nobody123
reject Exception
# row text: the queue's "That player does not exist" is for a name lookup; with the selector it is "No player was found"

## SQ-WO-04 | stays awake by day at the default random tick speed (r1109 ran at 300: tired-roll suspicion)
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> time set noon
> weather clear 100000
> setblock 30040 -60 30020 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak
sleep 120
> zwo state 30040 -60 30020
waitlog \[zwo\] done 20
> data get block 30040 -60 30020 creativeworldgen_sleep_until
sleep 1
expect \[zwo\] 30040 -60 30020 .*state=(none|blinking)
reject \[zwo\] 30040 -60 30020 .*state=sleeping
look if sleeping: does the data get show a sleep_until (tired sleep timer) or none (day sleep inject not active)?

## SQ-WO-06 | sleeps in a storm by day, wakes after (default tick speed, timer read)
> time set noon
> setblock 30050 -60 30020 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak
> weather thunder 600
sleep 120
> zwo state 30050 -60 30020
waitlog \[zwo\] done 20
> weather clear 100000
sleep 120
> zwo state 30050 -60 30020
waitlog \[zwo\] done 20
> data get block 30050 -60 30020 creativeworldgen_sleep_until
sleep 1
expect \[zwo\] 30050 -60 30020 .*state=sleeping
expect \[zwo\] 30050 -60 30020 .*state=(none|blinking)
look if the last state is sleeping: a sleep_until in the data get means a timed (tired) sleep, not the storm branch

## SQ-WO-08 | right-click on a sleeper: angry, 600 tick timer (r1109: tree was awake at the click; state read at each step)
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 0
> time set noon
> weather clear 100000
> setblock 30060 -60 30020 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak[state=sleeping]
> zwo state 30060 -60 30020
> wiseoak trust 30060 -60 30020 G 50
sleep 1
> zwo state 30060 -60 30020
> tp G 30060 -60 30017
> pbot use G 30060 -60 30020 up
> zwo state 30060 -60 30020
> data get block 30060 -60 30020 creativeworldgen_angry_until
sleep 1
waitlog \[zwo\] done 20
expect \[zwo\] 30060 -60 30020 .*state=angry
expect has the following block data
look angry_until = game + 600 within 5 ticks; if not angry, which zwo state line first reads awake (after setblock, after the trust command, or only after the use)

## SQ-WO-08b | same at midnight (diagnostic: a placed sleeper by day may wake on its first block-entity tick)
> time set midnight
> setblock 30070 -60 30020 mysticaloaktree:wise_oak[state=sleeping]
> wiseoak trust 30070 -60 30020 G 50
sleep 1
> zwo state 30070 -60 30020
> tp G 30070 -60 30017
> pbot use G 30070 -60 30020 up
> zwo state 30070 -60 30020
> data get block 30070 -60 30020 creativeworldgen_angry_until
sleep 1
waitlog \[zwo\] done 20
look RECORD: state before and after the use at night; angry here but not in -08 means the noon setblock wakes it (row text, not the inject)
> time set noon

## SQ-WO-09 | anger ends in a timed sleep on the game-time basis (tree of SQ-WO-08; meaningful only if -08 read angry)
> zwo skip 601
sleep 3
> zwo state 30060 -60 30020
> data get block 30060 -60 30020 creativeworldgen_sleep_until
> time add 12000
> data get block 30060 -60 30020 creativeworldgen_sleep_until
> time set noon
> zwo skip 12000
sleep 3
> zwo state 30060 -60 30020
sleep 1
waitlog \[zwo\] done 20
expect \[zwo\] 30060 -60 30020 .*state=sleeping
expect \[zwo\] 30060 -60 30020 .*state=(none|blinking)
look sleep_until = game + 12000 within 25 ticks, same value after time add; final state awake

## SQ-WO-35t | Wise Oak biome tag holds plains and forest, not taiga, desert, snowy plains, ocean, river, dripstone caves
> zq biometag creativeworldgen:wise_oak_biomes
waitlog \[zq\] done 20
expect \[zq\] biometag creativeworldgen:wise_oak_biomes \(\d+\):.* minecraft:plains\b
expect \[zq\] biometag creativeworldgen:wise_oak_biomes \(\d+\):.* minecraft:forest\b
reject \[zq\] biometag .* minecraft:(taiga|desert|snowy_plains|ocean|river|dripstone_caves)\b
# placement half (131 Wise Oaks, 129 in tagged biomes) was judged PASS offline in r1111

## SQ-HCS-05 | generated nest refills one crow per 5 game minutes up to 3, none with the player 60 away
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> fill 30495 -61 29995 30525 -45 30025 minecraft:glass hollow
> fill 30496 -60 29996 30524 -46 30024 minecraft:air
> setblock 30510 -55 30010 minecraft:oak_log
> setblock 30510 -54 30010 hearthandharvest:nest[generated=true]
> kill @e[type=hearthandharvest:crow]
> pbot spawn hcs5 30505 -60 30010 minecraft:overworld creative
sleep 2
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 300
repeat 5
> zwo skip 6100
sleep 8
> execute positioned 30510 -54 30010 if entity @e[type=hearthandharvest:crow,distance=..24]
end
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
expect Test passed, count: 1\b
expect Test passed, count: 3\b
reject Test passed, count: [4-9]
> kill @e[type=hearthandharvest:crow]
> tp hcs5 30570 -60 30010
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 300
> zwo skip 6100
sleep 10
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> execute positioned 30510 -54 30010 if entity @e[type=hearthandharvest:crow,distance=..24]
expect Test failed|Test passed, count: 0
> pbot remove hcs5
look the five counts rise one at a time (1, 2, 3, 3, 3) and never pass 3; last count 0 with the bot 60 blocks away

